                <pb facs="0821" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00/300: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-06T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 7, 7.44 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>During the last few days Belgium, Bolivia, Ecuador, France and Italy have
                    recognized the Peruvian Government. Uruguay and England have recognized the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
